# Hardware CD / media helpers (C:\DRIVERS\HW\)

Every pack ships **all** helpers so you can move a VHD between systems.

| Target | CD / media command | Audio init |
|--------|-------------------|------------|
| **mister** | `CALL imgtry …` or `CALL C:\DRIVERS\HW\IMGTRY.BAT …` | `PMINIT /SB` or `/GUS` + BLASTER/ULTRASND |
| **picogus** | `CALL C:\DRIVERS\HW\PGUSCD.BAT list\|load n\|eject` | BLASTER/ULTRASND; `PGUSINIT` mode; card firmware |
| **picomem** | BIOS disk select for VHD/IMG; `PMCD.BAT` stub for CD | `C:\PICOMEM\PMINIT.EXE /SB 1` or `/GUS 1` |
| **picoide** | Same helpers as PicoGUS (future) | TBD (pgusinit-like) |

## PicoGUS USB images

1. Build still stages pack sibling `cd/<game>/` with ISO/CUE files.
2. Copy those images to a **FAT32 USB stick root** (no subfolders).
3. Use `PGUSCD list` / `PGUSCD load n` (or `PGUSINIT /cdlist` / `/cdload n`).
4. See pack `cd\INDEX.TXT` for suggested index order (alphabetical like firmware).

## Drivers also on this VHD

- `C:\DRIVERS\PICOGUS\` — CDMKE.SYS, PGUSINIT.EXE  
- `C:\PICOMEM\` — PMINIT, PMEMM, PMDFS, PMMOUSE, SBCD, …  
- `C:\ULTRASND\` — GUS software tree (when staged)  
- `C:\DRIVERS\` — XCDROM, SHSUCDX, SBCTL, CTMOUSE, IMGTRY, …

Full reference: docs/NATIVE_PC_PACK.md in ExoDOSConverter.
